--- a/defaults/AGENTS.md
+++ b/defaults/AGENTS.md
@@ -956,8 +956,11 @@ the same limits, previews and removal as picked images.
 `.id("card").on_drag(payload, label)` makes an element draggable inside the
 window (a string payload up to 8 KiB; a chip shows `label`, default the payload's
 first line). Dropped on a space's group in the agents panel (grouped by space) or its row in the
-spaces panel, it reaches this mod's `nextDrop()` as `{ payload, space }` (`space`
-as `spaces()` lists it): one copy that is waiting gets it, any copy, so a popup
+spaces panel, it reaches this mod's `nextDrop()` as `{ payload, space, index }` (`space`
+as `spaces()` lists it; `index`: where among its tabs, before that position, 1 = first, null for the space as a
+whole). In the agents panel grouped by space, a space's header and every agent row under it take drops (a line
+shows where: the header is first, a row is right after its tab), and a row drags to another place in its group
+(`tab.move`): one copy that is waiting gets it, any copy, so a popup
 that started the drag may close. Keep the loop waiting:
 `cx.spawn(async (cx) => { for (;;) { const d = await nextDrop(); this.make(d); cx.notify(); } })`.
 A press that starts such a drag doesn't move a `window` overlay or a `window_drag` area.
